# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, regardless of the platform a
# clone happens on. Two concrete reasons this matters here rather than being a
# style preference:
#
#   * data/pinned_universes_manifest.json records a raw sha256 of each price CSV
#     alongside an LF-normalised one. Letting git rewrite CSVs to CRLF on
#     checkout makes the raw checksum unreproducible for Windows clones.
#   * The .pt checkpoints and .png plots must never be touched by any text
#     filter; a single CRLF substitution inside a tensor corrupts it silently.
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary -- no eol conversion, no diff.
*.pt   binary
*.pth  binary
*.png  binary
*.zip  binary
*.ipynb -text

# Data files: keep LF so the manifest checksums hold everywhere.
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
